.TH "PB-TEAM-BUCKET-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-bucket-remove - Disconnect the team's bucket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team bucket remove <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Disconnect the team's bucket. Paperboat forgets the stored access key and stops giving machines and browsers links to it. What the bucket already holds stays there for the team to manage, and terminal recordings stay on their machines, where they can still be replayed while the machine is online.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-bucket(1)\fP
